Chapter: CSV RFC 4180 Test
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Encode chapter Csv

 Csv against RFC 4180, in both directions.

 The grammar is record = field *(COMMA field). A separator is always
 followed by a field and that field may be empty, so a record ending
 in a comma has an empty last field and a record that is one comma
 has two of them. Those two were the defect: the row loop ended at
 the input without recording that it had just stepped over a
 separator, so the final empty field was never pushed.

 The other five parse lines are the control. They were correct before
 the fix and must stay correct, which is what separates a repair from
 a rewrite that moves everything.

 The emit lines are checked the other way round. Each was fed to an
 independent CSV parser on the host, which must recover exactly the
 fields that went in; quoting only when required, and doubling an
 embedded quote, are what that parser is being asked to confirm. A
 round trip through this chapter's own two halves would prove neither,
 because both halves can share an assumption and agree forever.

Section: Render

  render-fields : List Text, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  render-fields (fs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else render-fields fs (i + 1) n (acc & "[" & list-at fs i & "]")

  render-row : List Text -> Text
  render-row (fs) = "n=" & show (list-length fs) & " " & render-fields fs 0 (list-length fs) ""

  render-table : List (List Text) -> Text
  render-table (t) =
    if list-length t == 0 then "rows=0"
    else "rows=" & show (list-length t) & " " & render-row (list-at t 0)

  probe : Text -> Text
  probe (s) = render-table (csv-parse s)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("plain=" & probe "a,b,c")
    print-line-uni ("trailing=" & probe "a,")
    print-line-uni ("leading=" & probe ",a")
    print-line-uni ("middle=" & probe "a,,b")
    print-line-uni ("qcomma=" & probe "\"x,y\",z")
    print-line-uni ("qquote=" & probe "\"he said \"\"hi\"\"\",z")
    print-line-uni ("bare-comma=" & probe ",")
    print-line-uni ("emit-plain=" & csv-emit-row ["a", "b"])
    print-line-uni ("emit-comma=" & csv-emit-row ["x,y", "z"])
    print-line-uni ("emit-quote=" & csv-emit-row ["he said \"hi\"", "z"])
    print-line-uni ("emit-trailing=" & csv-emit-row ["a", ""])
    print-line-uni ("emit-both-empty=" & csv-emit-row ["", ""])
  end

